  <content>
    <description>
      <levelledPara id="par-000012-01">
        <title>Warnings</title>
        <warning>
          <warningAndCautionPara>Dangerous voltages are present in the PDU-200 when mains power is connected. Make sure the main circuit breaker is open and tagged before you start. If you do not, you can be killed or seriously injured.</warningAndCautionPara>
        </warning>
        <warning>
          <warningAndCautionPara>The power supply modules can stay hot for up to 15 minutes after power is removed. Wear protective gloves when you handle them.</warningAndCautionPara>
        </warning>
        <para>Obey the warnings above when you work on the radar power system. Each procedure in this publication repeats the warnings that apply to it.</para>
      </levelledPara>
      <levelledPara id="par-000012-02">
        <title>Cautions</title>
        <caution>
          <warningAndCautionPara>The power supply modules contain parts that electrostatic discharge can damage. Wear a grounded wrist strap when you handle a module.</warningAndCautionPara>
        </caution>
        <caution>
          <warningAndCautionPara>Do not force a module into its slot. Damage to the rear connector can occur.</warningAndCautionPara>
        </caution>
        <para>Obey these cautions to prevent damage to the equipment.</para>
      </levelledPara>
    </description>
